A||||2||FIEROCIOUS||EGR solenoid delete wireing???||||1||
Z||000000||FIEROCIOUS||07-18-2000||03:56 PM||||I've looked at ALL posts containing information about EGR's and the like. I can't find a thread on how to rewire the EGR solenoid wires when you remove the solenoid.<P>I remember someone saying they took the solenoid off and soldered the wires so the computer wouldn't trip a code. I would like to do this before I start my new engine and begine testing.<P>Who wrote that or does anyone know how to do this?<P>I have an air/fuel meter and a pyrometer hooked up to my car and am trying to solve the EGR debate without bias. I appreciate your help.||||reg||1
Z||000001||ka4nkf||07-18-2000||05:26 PM||||ThereIs two small black wires by the vac lines. tey are real close together, side by side. They go to the vac switch, pull these two wires out and tie together. they have spade terminals so they will come out. with these two wires tied together this makes the computer think the switch is made up and the EGR is working ok, so you will not get a code 32. If you remove the solenoid completely, then I dont know which wires you tie together on the main plug. I have not removed mine I just left It on and tied the wires like I said. No more code 32 and runs great. als my EGR valve Is pluged off.||||reg||1
Z||000002||FIEROCIOUS||07-19-2000||02:26 AM||||Thank you very much! Just what I was looking for!!!!!<P>-Mike||||reg||1
